BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Fat\, Sexy\, and Free at Come As You Are
DTSTART:20260615T190000
DTEND:20260615T190000
UID:aebcb5d62a645e968c2b383cdb2a2c4c@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:EVERY BODY IS A SEXY BODY. BUT WE&#x27\;VE BEEN LIED TO ABOUT 
 SEXINESS. What have you learned about &#x27\;sexiness&#x27\;? Why is it so
  hard to feel sexy? How do you move from shame to more pleasure in this bo
 dy... in THIS body\, RIGHT now. Fat\, plus size\, chubby\, voluptuous\, vo
 luminous\, BBW/BHM\, Queen/King/Royalty sized. Feeling more sexy in a fat 
 body means we have can feel more fun\, satisfaction and joy in our sex. Se
 xual confidence isn&#x27\;t a look - it&#x27\;s an unlearning of desirabil
 ity and a reclaiming of the power of presence. -- Luna Matatas\, Sex and P
 leasure Educator I have spent a decade unlearning fatphobia\, body shame a
 nd oppressive beauty standards. I am sharing tools and techniques to help 
 you explore sexiness on your own terms\, and find more body freedom in the
  process. Body shame doesn&#x27\;t fuel confidence\, and can create barrie
 rs to pleasure in the bedroom. We may avoid positions\, fantasies and comm
 unication that we feel self-conscious in. Set that shame free and make roo
 m for more pleasure in my class. We’ll cover topics like: Sex position p
 leasure for fat bodies - get on top or face sit with confidence Toys and t
 ools for better sex Shopping tips for lingerie and accessories Fetishizati
 on of fat bodies vs. adoration Reclaiming our gaze Navigating shame and pe
 rformance anxiety Exploring empowered approaches to dating\, attraction an
 d desire Asking for what we want and how to own our &#x27\;no&#x27\; You&#
 x27\;ll leave the class equipped with practices\, rituals and ideas to hel
 p you navigate connection\, confidence and physical challenges with more e
 ase. ‍ ‍
LOCATION:Come as You Are\, 254 Augusta Ave
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/fat-sexy-and-free-at-come-as-you-are
X-SOURCE:YOHOMO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Thank God I&#x27\;m A Lesbian: A Dykeumentary Screening
DTSTART:20260615T193000
DTEND:20260615T193000
UID:5e29bd9e37b88bbb98f8af663834ca55@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:A monthly lesbian movie night\, Pride month edition\, featurin
 g a documentary about the diversity of lesbian identities. This one is clo
 se to home! Dykeumentary Night is a monthly lesbian movie night focusing o
 n showcasing and shining light on lesbian and dyke documentaries and those
  who make them. For our first ever Pride edition\, we are showcasing 1992 
 film &quot\;Thank God I&#x27\;m A Lesbian.&quot\; Come alone\, leave with 
 friends. This is a true community. Each ticket comes with popcorn. ABOUT T
 HE MOVIE THANK GOD I&#x27\;M A LESBIAN is an uplifting and entertaining do
 cumentary about the diversity of lesbian identities. Dionne Brand\, Nicole
  Brossard\, Lee Pui Ming\, Becki Ross\, Julia Creet\, LaVerne Monette\, Sa
 rah Schulman\, Chris Bearchell\, Chris Phibbs\, Christine Delphy and Jeane
 lle Laillou speak frankly and articulately about issues ranging from comin
 g out\, racism\, bisexuality\, and SM\, to the evolution of the feminist a
 nd lesbian movements\, outing and compulsory heterosexuality. Inclusive of
  various and often contradictory points of view\, THANK GOD I&#x27\;M A LE
 SBIAN successfully proposes an alternate vision of self and community that
  is realistic and positive. This fast-paced documentary was edited by Gera
 ldine Peroni who was nominated for an Academy Award for The Player. ABOUT 
 THE FILMMAKERS Dominique Cardona Born in Algeria\, Dominique Cardona moved
  to France at the age of seven and achieved a law degree from the Universi
 ty of Montpellier. She moved to Toronto in 1990 and attended the summer fi
 lm program of New York University. She made her directorial debut in 1992 
 with THANK GOD I&#x27\;M A LESBIAN. Cardona’s partner of 27 years\, Laur
 ie Colbert\, has worked together with Cardona on award winning films\, inc
 luding 2007’s FINN&#x27\;S GIRL. Most recently Cardona and Colbert have 
 moved into fiction storytelling. With their award winning MARGARITA\, made
  in 2012\, Colbert and Cardona explore political and social issues by tell
 ing the story of a young\, immigrant nanny working for a family in Canada.
  (8/14) Laurie Colbert Colbert was born in Canada in 1958. Her interest in
  film peaked when she became involved with various LGBT groups. Colbert an
 d her partner of 27 years\, Dominique Cardona\, worked together on many aw
 ard winning films\, including THANK GOD I’M A LESBIAN and 2007’s FINN
 ’S GIRL. The focus of Colbert’s work is uplifting stories about presen
 t-day struggles for the LGBT community. Most recently Cardona and Colbert 
 have moved into fiction storytelling. With their award winning MARGARITA\,
  made in 2012\, Colbert and Cardona explore political and social issues by
  telling the story of a young\, immigrant nanny working for a family in Ca
 nada. (8/14) Run time: 55 minutes any opinions and ideas expressed in movi
 es shown at this event do not reflect the ideas or opinions of Three Dolla
 r Bill or the organizer ‍
LOCATION:Three Dollar Bill\, 1592 Queen Street West
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/thank-god-im-a-lesbian-a-dykeumentary-scre
 ening
X-SOURCE:YOHOMO
END:VEVENT
