 Pm Where: Three Dollar Bill Bar\, 1592 Queen St W\, Parkdale\, Toronto M6R
  1A8 Vibe: Low sensory\, masked\, creative &amp\; nerdy Cost: [FREE/PRICE]
  Dress Code: MASKED! Craft Your Own Variant Cover! CALLING ALL TRANS &amp\
 ; SAPPHIC COMIC NERDS! Don your mask and join us at HQ (Three Dollar Bill)
  on June 21st for a low-sensory creative night! We&#x27\;re diving deep in
 to comic book culture with a collage-making session. Quest Details: Masked
  Collage Workshop - Comics Theme - Channel your favorite artists and creat
 e! Make your own comic panel sequences\, design variant covers\, craft cha
 racter mood boards\, build your dream crossover event\, or reimagine class
 ic scenes. We&#x27\;ll have comic books\, graphic novels\, manga\, and art
  supplies ready for you to cut\, paste\, and create your masterpiece while
  protecting your own secrets identity. preferred quieter creative space du
 ring such a bustling Pride season. Info-Dump Friendly Zone - Chat about yo
 ur favorite runs\, debate the best comic book adaptations\, discuss the su
 perior Robin\, argue about retcons\, or just geek out about panel composit
 ion and storytelling techniques with people who actually care about the di
 fference between DC&#x27\;s Crisis events. Whether you&#x27\;re a Marvel d
 evotee\, DC loyalist\, manga collector\, indie comic enthusiast\, webcomic
  reader\, or just someone who has Opinions™ about the MCU this is YOUR s
 pace! Meet fellow nerds who GET IT\, find people who know their Deadpool v
 ariants from their Spider-Verse issues\, and vibe with creative queers in 
 a chill\, low-sensory environment. All skill levels welcome. No gatekeepin
 g allowed. Art supplies &amp\; comics provided—but bring your own favori
 tes to sacrifice to the collage gods! Low sensory environment: Softer ligh
 ting\, quieter space for focused creating\, masks to keep everyone safe! S
 pace is not Wheelchair Accessible\, No ASL interpreter. ‍
