BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Groundwork 08
DTSTART:20260621T183000
DTEND:20260621T183000
UID:fd39deefa47a0aabcc8908cc3adb748f@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:Groundwork is a generative workshop space for queer writers. l
 ay the groundwork Idiom To provide the right conditions Groundwork is a ge
 nerative workshop series in Toronto aiming to provide space for queer writ
 ers to access writing time and a writing community\, away from institution
 alized pressures or expectations. We&#x27\;re back in Toronto! This eighth
  iteration of Groundwork returns to Grape Witches upstairs salon on June 2
 1st\, 2026 from 6:30 - 8:30pm. The structure of the workshop is designed t
 o provide an hour to an hour and a half of writing time\, with guided inte
 ractive prompts. The last half-hour will be reserved for chilling\, chatti
 ng and connecting — feel free to migrate to Grape Witches downstairs aft
 er this! Our workshop is not bound by any writing style\, genre or previou
 s achievements. We wish to welcome all writers at all points in their lite
 rary journey. Please bring paper and writing utensils! Tickets are PWYC (r
 ecommended amount $5-10) and go directly to paying for the salon space. No
  one will be turned away for lack of funds. We look forward to hosting you
  ❤️ ******************************************************************
 **************************************** Grape Witches is a leader in dive
 rsifying and democratizing Toronto’s wine scene. We’ve added a couple 
 of words from their home page for those who are unfamiliar with the space.
  We began as\, and always will be\, industry veterans on a mission. Founde
 d in 2015\, Grape Witches began as a series of parties and educational eve
 nts pouring the rare and delicious organic\, biodynamic and natural wine w
 e loved. The dream? To share the incredible flavours\, places and people t
 hat made us work in wine - without the stuffy attitude. Fast forward throu
 gh a few hundred parties big and small\; from geeky winemaker events to sw
 eaty dance parties to the world&#x27\;s largest natural wine booze cruise 
 (yes\, actually!!)\, and you&#x27\;ll find us on March 7th 2020 (lol) sign
 ing the lease to our first space and launching our natural wine agency\, G
 rape Witch Imports. ‍
LOCATION:Grape Witches\, 1247 Dundas Street W
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/groundwork-08
X-SOURCE:YOHOMO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Party &amp\; Play
DTSTART:20260621T203000
DTEND:20260621T203000
UID:5391be8bcd32a0169f92263e5269d94a@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:Are your friends dragging you to another Woody’s dance party
  where the drinks are $25 and the music is just more Lady Gaga remixes? Lo
 ok – no shade!! All hail Gaga\, etc\, etc. But pride is the most joyous 
 time of year in Toronto\, and joy comes in many different forms… Like 
 “Party &amp\; Play!” – the queerest\, most joyful comedy show of 202
 6\, featuring some of Toronto’s best queer talent. Hosted by the incredi
 ble Hillary Yass &amp\; Selena Vyle\, this variety show celebrates Pride t
 hrough the lens of the everyday gay lifestyle\, bringing you stand-up\, sk
 etch comedy\, improv and drag all done by incredibly successful 2SLGBTQ+ m
 embers of the Toronto comedy scene\, including: Kirsten Rasmussen\, Brando
 n Hackett\, Anders Yates\, Tyra Banda\, Ben Sosa-Wright\, Zoe Marin\, Blai
 r MacMillan\, Robert Defina\, Stevey Hunter\, A.C. Birch\, Tony Varkaris\,
  Phil Johnston\, Katie Chin\, Kirk McCullough and Adam Urquhart ! By the e
 nd of the show\, the whole cast will get together and deliver one of the m
 ost iconic gay improv montages of all time\, inspired by your suggestions 
 and stories! You’ll be gooped\, gagged and… something else that starts
  with a g! Comedy ain’t just a straight man’s game no more\, y’all! 
 ‍
LOCATION:Second City Toronto\, 1 York St
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/party-play
X-SOURCE:YOHOMO
