BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:It Takes a Village Walking Tour
DTSTART:20260624T183000
DTEND:20260624T183000
UID:b8f6c16e6c73e468c1fcf4d61dc95f19@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:Join us on a guided walk through Church-Wellesley Village to e
 xplore the powerful legacy of Toronto’s 2SLGBTQ+ community and learn abo
 ut efforts to strengthen the neighbourhood today and build the community f
 or the future. From the resilience shown during the Bathhouse Raids and th
 e AIDS epidemic to the joy and connection found at spaces like the Buddies
  in Bad Times Theatre and the St. Charles Tavern\, this tour traces the la
 ndmarks of both struggle and celebration. This emerging historian tour wil
 l be led by Ella Miller\, a local writer and editor who specializes in rep
 orting on queerness\, disability\, and rural living. A recent graduate fro
 m Toronto Metropolitan University with a Bachelor’s of Journalism and a 
 minor in 2SLGBTQIA+ studies\, Ella has led tours at the Old Stone Mill Nat
 ional Historic Site in Delta\, Ontario\, and the Rogers Centre with the To
 ronto Blue Jays. Ella is passionate about local history and has been invol
 ved in archival and education work since she was 10 years old. ‍
LOCATION:Barbara Hall Park\, 519 Church Street
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/it-takes-a-village-walking-tour-4
X-SOURCE:YOHOMO
END:VEVENT
